<https://w3id.org/tesseract/industrial-crosswalks/cfihos-ifc> a sssom:MappingSet ;
    rdfs:label "CFIHOS V2.0 property dictionary to IFC4 ADD2 property and quantity machinery" ;
    rdfs:comment "SCOPE, STATED UP FRONT: the open CFIHOS OWL exposes a PROPERTY DICTIONARY, 1,388 classes such as 'shell wall thickness' and 'upper limit design pressure', not a labelled equipment taxonomy in owl:Class form. So this is a crosswalk at the PROPERTY layer and nowhere else, and an equipment-class crosswalk between CFIHOS and IFC is not authorable from the open artefacts. THE FINDING: CFIHOS names 1,388 process-plant properties; IFC names roughly a dozen generic quantity and property constructs. The mapping is therefore MANY-TO-ONE INTO A GENERIC SLOT. Going CFIHOS to IFC loses the name and keeps the number; going IFC to CFIHOS is not determined at all. That asymmetry is the plant-to-building handover problem stated exactly. Exact normalised token overlap between the two class sets is ONE name. CFIHOS is an IOGP publication; this references the Universidad de Murcia OWL rendering and restates no IOGP material. Confidence is the curator's judgement." ;
    sssom:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
    sssom:mapping_set_id <https://w3id.org/tesseract/industrial-crosswalks/cfihos-ifc> ;
    sssom:mapping_set_version "0.1.0" .

